# INT-SOURCE: ../functional/88_dict_temp_reads.my
# INT-ENGINES: tw default nj noopt
#
# INT unit (#107) over tests/functional/88_dict_temp_reads.my:
# a read through a dict no variable holds (a call's result, a literal,
# an element read as a value) gets the entry's value - the tree-walker
# handed out a pointer into a dict that died before the read - while a
# default dict reached through such a handle still takes its new key,
# and a default dict's `d.k` read inserts the default in every engine.
#
# It runs as a coverage unit under the engines above, with no second
# copy (INT-SOURCE): code no other unit reaches. It asserts its own
# results, and every engine must print the same.
